SUMMARY:Meet Your Plant Neighbors
DESCRIPTION:Join TLC for an exploration of plants at Old Creedmoor Nature Preserve!\nWhich plants do we live amongst? What are their names? What are their stories? On this 1.4-mile hike\, we will celebrate Public Lands Day by meeting our plant neighbors at TLC's newest preserve\, Old Creedmoor. We'll amble along Lizard's Tail Loop identifying trees\, shrubs\, and herbs along the way. All levels of plant knowledge are welcome -- we are a community of learners and sharers!\n\nThis is a free event\, but preregistration is required. The group will return to the parking lot by sunset\, but please bring a flashlight or headlamp just in case visibility begins to lower at the end of the hike.\n\n \n \nIf registration is full\, please fill out the waitlist form here by September 24th at noon.
URL:https://triangleland.org/event/meet-your-plant-neighbors-3
LOCATION:Old Creedmoor Nature Preserve\, 13509 Old Creedmoor Rd\, Wake Forest\, NC\, 27587\, United States
ORGANIZER;CN="Amaya Horner":MAILTO:ahorner@triangleland.org
END:VEVENT
